            <div xml:id="d388-a11">

                <pb facs="0740" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg678"/>

                <p rendition="#center">(Deposited at Reynosa April 29, 1878. Received at city of
                    Mexico same day at 11.3<hi rendition="#superscript">5</hi> a.m.)</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Messrs. Martinez and A. Perales:</p>
                <p>Below Nueva Laredo, at Las Estacas, a band of savage Indians have crossed. They
                    were armed, and had 400 stolen animals with them. Commandant Estebun Ramos has
                    gone to give them a thrashing. I am awaiting the result. The invasion of the
                    Indians occurs coincidently with that of the Lerdists below this point.</p>
                <closer><signed>S. CANALES.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The foregoing are copies.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1878-06-08">June 8,
                            1878</date>.</dateline>
                        <lb/>
                        <signed>JOSÉ T. DE CUELLAR,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
